   "answer": "## Result (corrected): MIC50 and MIC90 for nine drugs against 110 *Mycoplasma anserisalpingitidis* strains\n\n**Scope**\n- Standard: none. The species has no clinical breakpoints, so I did not read the results as susceptible (S), intermediate (I) or resistant (R).\n- Isolates: 110 strains. Each strain gives one MIC value per drug.\n- Units: µg/mL, which equals mg/L.\n- Tool: AMR summary tool, which reports AMR version 3.0.1.\n\n**What I did**\n1. I read the MIC table directly. The inspection tool failed.\n2. I ran the MIC summary tool on all nine drugs. MIC50 and MIC90 are the lowest concentrations that inhibit at least 50% and at least 90% of the strains.\n3. I kept values with a limit sign, such as ≤0.25 or >64, at their limit. The tool used the next dilution only for the geometric mean.\n4. I recalculated the extreme-value flags with a script, on the raw scale and on the log2 scale.\n\n**Results (n = 110 strains per drug)**\n\n| Drug | MIC50 (µg/mL) | MIC90 (µg/mL) | Range (µg/mL) | Geometric mean (µg/mL) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Tilmicosin | 64 | >64 | ≤0.25 to >64 | 21.93 |\n| Tylosin | 16 | 64 | ≤0.25 to >64 | 6.55 |\n| Tylvalosin | 0.5 | 2 | ≤0.25 to 16 | 0.66 |\n| Lincomycin | 2 | 4 | 0.5 to >64 | 2.74 |\n| Oxytetracycline | 16 | 64 | ≤0.25 to 64 | 11.85 |\n| Doxycycline | 5 | 10 | ≤0.039 to >10 | 2.32 |\n| Spectinomycin | 8 | 16 | 4 to >64 | 10.62 |\n| Enrofloxacin | 5 | >10 | 0.312 to 16 | 4.92 |\n| Tiamulin | 0.625 | 2.5 | 0.078 to 2.5 | 0.65 |\n\n**Values at the limit of the dilution series (count of strains)**\n- Tilmicosin: 16 at ≤0.25 and 24 at >64.\n- Tylosin: 20 at ≤0.25 and 5 at >64.\n- Tylvalosin: 33 at ≤0.25.\n- Lincomycin: 1 at >64.\n- Oxytetracycline: 2 at ≤0.25.\n- Doxycycline: 1 at ≤0.039 and 2 at >10.\n- Spectinomycin: 1 at >64.\n- Enrofloxacin: 25 at >10.\n- Tiamulin: none.\n\n**What the results show**\n- Tylvalosin and Tiamulin have the lowest MIC50 and MIC90 values in this set.\n- Tilmicosin has the highest MIC50 and MIC90 values. Its MIC90 is above the top of the series.\n- Enrofloxacin MIC90 is above the top of the series (>10 µg/mL).\n- These are laboratory MIC values. They do not show that a drug works for a patient.\n\n**Extreme-value flags: correction**\n- The harness data check reported extreme values with a modified z-score above 3.5. Its counts were Tylosin 7, Tylvalosin 4, Lincomycin 6 and Tiamulin 12. I could not reproduce these counts.\n- My recalculation on the raw scale gave Tylvalosin 19, Lincomycin 7, Tiamulin 12 and 0 for the other drugs.\n- My recalculation on the log2 scale gave Tylosin 20, Oxytetracycline 3, Doxycycline 4 and 0 for the other drugs.\n- For Tilmicosin and Spectinomycin the median absolute deviation is 0, so the rule cannot score any value.\n- The flagged sets change with the scale. They do not show clear data errors.\n- I removed the total of 29 from the earlier answer. I do not report a total, because it depends on the scale.\n- I kept all values in the data.\n\n**What is uncertain**\n- Values at a limit sign are counted at the limit. The true MIC can lie beyond it.\n- The 110 rows are one row per strain. The file does not show the host bird, flock or herd. If several strains come from one source, they are not independent.\n- The file has one MIC per strain and drug. I cannot tell whether a value is one test or a mean of replicates.\n- The first row is the reference strain ATCC BAA-2147 (American Type Culture Collection). It is one of the 110 rows.\n- The summary tool reports AMR version 3.0.1. The program notes list 4.6.1. I cannot tell which version ran. MIC50 and MIC90 do not depend on breakpoint tables.\n\n**Output files**\n- Summary table: mic_summary-1/summary.csv in the project work folder.\n- Plot: mic_summary-1/plot.png, with an SVG copy.\n- Outlier checks: outlier_check.csv (raw scale) and outlier_check_log2.csv (log2 scale).\n\n**What waits for you**\n1. Decide whether to keep the ATCC BAA-2147 reference strain.\n2. Confirm whether the strains come from separate birds, flocks or herds.\n3. Confirm whether each MIC is one test or a mean of replicates.\n4. Choose the scale for the extreme-value rule (raw or log2), or keep all values. All values are kept now.\n5. Confirm which AMR version you ran.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n2 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/kovacs2026-mycoplasma-mic/run1/home/sessions/20261009-033411-7b04/work and wrote 1 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/kovacs2026-mycoplasma-mic/run1/home/sessions/20261009-033411-7b04/work.\n- n3 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/kovacs2026-mycoplasma-mic/run1/home/sessions/20261009-033411-7b04/work and wrote 1 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/kovacs2026-mycoplasma-mic/run1/home/sessions/20261009-033411-7b04/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Geometric mean of MIC values with a limit sign: next dilution.",
